Also, don't chase them, and accidentally attack them while blind and naked.
I just lost one of my best characters ever to a memory fault.  Excuse my
bragging, but this was a level 12 wizard on level 16.  I had 112 hit points
and was going to get more, a +7 Excalibur, armor class of -14, and most of
the intrinsics except teleport and teleport control.  I put on my blind-
fold so I could keep track of the other monsters on the level while I was
blind and unarmed.  I had just killed one of my previous ghosts, who had
a lot of good stuff, and so did I (amulet of lifesaving, 5 holy waters,
and a magic marker and some blank scrolls among other things).  I happened
on two nurses, and one of them disappeared.  I chased one, and got more
hit points.  She ran again, and I gave chase.  I accidentally bumped into
her, and bang, memory fault.  So where do I send bug reports?  This was on
a Sun Sparc 1+, SunOS 4.1.1.  I am the system administrator and the game
maintainer.  I am during finals week (hell of a way to study, huh), or I
would go into wizard mode and try to track down the bug.  I have a feeling
it is in either the player attack or monster attack code.  Damn it.  I
might have finally ascended with this character, since I had not run into
anything that could screw with me, and had lifesaving.

